<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="dark">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  
  {# SEO Meta Tags #}
  {% include "partials/seo-meta.njk" %}
  
  {# Preconnect hints for fonts #}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  
  {# Font loading with swap for no FOIT #}
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  
  {# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Critical above-the-fold CSS (Requirements 18.7, 25.2, 5.6)
     Inlined to paint the dark theme, font stacks, sticky header/nav, and
     hero baseline immediately — eliminating the render-blocking round-trip
     to the main stylesheet and preventing FOUC / layout shift (CLS).
     Keep this minimal: only what is visible before scroll.
     ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <style>
    /* Reset + dark theme base */
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    :root {
      --background: #0A0A0A;
      --foreground: #F5F5F5;
      --muted-foreground: #888888;
      --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      --accent: #f59e0b; /* bright amber - nav active */
      color-scheme: dark;
    }
    html {
      background: #0A0A0A;
      color: #F5F5F5;
      font-size: 16px;
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
    }
    /* ─── Font fallback strategy (Requirements 25.2, 5.6) ───────────────
       The Google Fonts <link>s above use `&display=swap`, so the browser
       paints text immediately in the system fallback (no FOIT) and swaps in
       the web font once loaded.

       To avoid layout shift (CLS) on swap OR on total web-font failure, the
       fallback stacks below are chosen to be metric-compatible with the web
       fonts: the leading system UI faces (system-ui / -apple-system / Segoe
       UI / Roboto) have x-height and advance widths very close to Inter, and
       the leading monospace faces (ui-monospace / SF Mono / Menlo) closely
       match JetBrains Mono's fixed advance. Because all monospace glyphs share
       one advance width, the mono fallback is effectively metric-identical.

       These two stacks MUST stay byte-for-byte identical to the ones declared
       in src/css/components.css (html / code) so the inlined critical CSS and
       the async main bundle never disagree and re-flow text. If you change one,
       change the other. (No `size-adjust` @font-face is needed because the
       fallbacks are already metric-compatible; document any future override
       here alongside the matching components.css change.) */
    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-width: 320px;
      overflow-x: hidden;
      min-height: 100vh;
      background: var(--background);
      color: var(--foreground);
      font-family: "Inter", system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
    }
    code, pre, .font-mono {
      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", "Fira Code", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    }
    /* Sticky header / nav baseline (matches header.njk: fixed, h-16 = 64px) */
    [data-sticky-nav] {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      z-index: 50;
      height: 4rem;
      transition: transform 0.3s ease, background-color 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease;
    }
    [data-sticky-nav] nav {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      height: 4rem;
      max-width: 1440px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      padding-right: 1.5rem;
    }
    /* Hero baseline — large bold headline, prevents jump before full CSS loads */
    h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
    img, svg, video { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
    a { color: inherit; }
  </style>

  {# Main CSS bundle — preloaded then applied async to avoid render-blocking,
     with a <noscript> fallback for clients without JavaScript. #}
  <link rel="preload" href="/css/styles.css" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css"></noscript>
  
  {# Favicon #}
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/images/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon">
</head>
<body class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground antialiased">
  {# Skip to content link for keyboard users (visually hidden until focused) #}
  <a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>

  {{ content | safe }}
  
  {# Deferred JavaScript #}
  <script type="module" src="/js/main.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
